Paper presents the study conducted in Mokotów district in Warsaw, encompassing circular practices of eight chosen local entities, from private, public and NGO sectors. The choice was based on the preliminary research showing that the entities were already engaged in some form of the circular transition. The definition of the circular economy applied in the study was based on the one proposed by Kircherr, Reike and Hekkert describing a circular economy as an economic system based on business models replacing the ‘end-of-life’ concept with reducing, alternatively reusing, recycling and recovering materials in production/distribution and consumption processes. The aim is to accomplish sustainable development, by creating environmental quality, economic prosperity and social equity, to the benefit of current and future generations. The goals of the study encompassed:
· verification if there is a common understanding of what circular economy is;
· identification and comparison of circular practices introduced by various actors;
· identification of existing incentives for the circular practices and expected benefits;
· pinpointing the obstacles and barriers, both within organizations and outside.
The identified practices were also verified to support more specific goals of circular economy, present in the literature. The findings shows that current benefits of circular transition are limited and the actions are mostly driven by personal involvement. Lack of the support of local administration is evident, as well as the limitation of the market solutions. Networking turns are to be one of the most important aspects of efficient circular practices.

Problematyka artykułu skupia się na wybranych aspektach dotyczących ekonomicznego i finansowego oblicza podatku od towarów i usług, ze szczególnym uwzględnieniem podatkowych uwarunkowań decyzji przedsiębiorstw.
Stąd w artykule przedstawiono m.in.:
1) zagadnienie neutralności (systemu podatkowego oraz samego podatku od wartości dodanej);
2) konsekwencje różnicowania zasad opodatkowania oraz zwolnień w VAT 1;
3) istotę przerzucalności podatku oraz jego wpływ na finanse przedsiębiorstw.
Wyselekcjonowano i przybliżono również najważniejsze kierunki zmian w podatku od towarów i usług z perspektywy przedsiębiorstw. Artykuł ma charakter teoretyczno-praktyczny, zastosowano w nim metodę studiów literaturowych oraz analizy aktów prawnych.

The chapter in analysed the variation of the synthetic variable defined as the dissemination of responsible management practices and verified its association between:
- location in regions with different levels of development; 
- time of operation in the market; 
- type of ownership capital; 
- size of the company; 
- extent of activity. 
Based on the data collected, the relationships between these variables were verified and their strength estimated using Cramer's V. Responsible management practices are part of the broader area of corporate social responsibility. In the studies carried out, despite the limitations related to their generalisation to the population of all enterprises in Poland, one can note similar to global trends in the dissemination of practices, which represent an ongoing change in the objectives and tasks that stakeholders put before enterprises.

The aim of the SLIM VAT packages is to remove obligations imposed on Polish entrepreneurs that are redundant and obsolete in the digital era. This is the third edition of this package. The SLIM VAT package 3 involves a range of changes that can be grouped for the purposes of this text as:
1) improving the financial liquidity of enterprises;
2) reducing the documentary requirements in international trade;
3) reducing the number of VAT corrections;
4) facilitating invoicing;
5) reducing VAT sanctions and
6) consolidating binding information.
